`status.value as TestStatusValue` is an unsafe lie to TypeScript. `statusValueToStoryIdsMap` only has keys for the five test-specific values (`pending`, `success`, `error`, `warning`, `unknown`). If `status.value` is `'status-value:new'`, `'status-value:modified'`, or `'status-value:affected'` — all of which are now valid `StatusValue` members — the map lookup returns `undefined`, and `.push()` on `undefined` throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined`. While the vitest addon does not currently set those values, any shared-status pipeline that mixes change-detection and test statuses in `allStatuses` would hit this. Replace the cast with a runtime guard:
```ts
if ((status.value as string) in statusValueToStoryIdsMap) {
  statusValueToStoryIdsMap[status.value as TestStatusValue].push(status.storyId);
}
```
